#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 285 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object extracts properties from the audio stream
by matching. Non-property values and the audio signal are passed through
untouched to the first outlet;
#X text 240 138 note: although audio connections in Pd usually carry
only audio signals \, they can also carry ordinary control messages
\, which are routed through the same patch cords. This is rare but
possible \, and the object takes such messages into account;
#X obj 230 143 cnv 1 2 75 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -158925 -1 0;
#X text 240 223 each matched property is output from its own outlet
without the property selector \, unmatched properties are output from
the last outlet;
#X text 240 278 the object can be used to extract parameter values
that travel through audio connections \, for example to read the current
value of a property from a GUI object while the audio signal continues
through the patch;
